This skill is a bilingual fork; its parts carry different authorship.

- The English detection layer ("English AI-isms" and the language-agnostic
  structural rules in SKILL.md, plus references/english-phrase-rules.md) is
  rebased verbatim from "avoid-ai-writing" by Conor Bronsdon, licensed under the
  MIT License. That upstream copyright and permission notice is preserved in the
  LICENSE file in this directory.

- The Traditional-Chinese layer ("Traditional Chinese AI-isms" and
  references/zh-phrase-rules.md) and the skill's own framing are original work
  by Lu Yi, MIT-licensed (see the repository-root LICENSE).

- Some Taiwan-usage entries in references/zh-phrase-rules.md (the 翻譯腔
  patterns) were informed by "speak-human-tw" by Raymond Hou (雷蒙三十),
  licensed under the MIT License. Those entries are our own rewrite, not copied
  text.

- evals/evals.json ids 15-54 adapt 40 of the 42 test cases from
  "speak-human-tw"'s evals/benchmark.md by Raymond Hou (雷蒙三十), licensed
  under the MIT License. Unlike the zh-phrase-rules.md entries above, this is
  a verbatim adaptation, not a rewrite: the source text (原文/問題點/預期方向)
  is reproduced as-is with added structural fields (bucket, 面向, 對應規則,
  tier) for this repo's eval format. Two cases (SF-14, SF-15 — 中國用語 and
  半形標點) were excluded as out of this skill's scope and noted for
  avoid-china-writing's backlog instead.
